# The N3 content tree is byte-checked by tests/content.n3.test.mjs, which
# rejects CRLF and requires a trailing LF.
#
# The backend is a Node/TypeScript project whose lint gate (eslint-config-google)
# enforces LF as well. Windows clones default to core.autocrlf=true, so pin the
# checked-out bytes instead of relying on each developer's git config.
networking-fundamentals/backend/content/** text eol=lf
networking-fundamentals/backend/** text eol=lf
